  "body": "What happens: `a_finer_pass_that_runs_out_on_a_face_that_may_jump_is_refused` in `crates/app/tests/import_step_guard.rs:36` failed in pr-test run 43533416032 (PR 1598) with \"import did not finish within 30s - the hang is back\". PR 1598 touches no import or STEP code; the self-hosted runner was running another gate and a post-merge run at the same time. Motion and ui suites passed.\n\nWhy it matters: the test pins the hang guard for untrusted STEP files with a wall-clock limit, so a busy runner turns an unrelated PR's quick gate red and the review cannot be proven by a build.\n\nNot proven: that load is the cause. No completed post-merge run on main shows the test green or red at that moment.\n\nWanted: the pin should not depend on machine load - assert on the guard's evaluation count (the metered budget) rather than wall time, or raise the limit well above the measured time on a loaded runner and keep one generous outer timeout as the hang barrier. The guard itself must not be weakened.\n\nDone means: the test passes on the runner while two other gates run, and still fails when the guard is removed (mutation check named in the PR).\n",
